  "worked_solution": "From the identity $1+{cot}^{2}\u2061\\theta ={csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta ,$ with $\\theta =5x-2,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{cot}^{2}\u2061(5x-2)={csc}^{2}\u2061(5x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{cot}^{2}\u2061(5x-2)\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(5x-2)+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(5x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{[{cot}^{2}\u2061(5x-2)+1]\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(5x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{csc}^{2}\u2061(5x-2)\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(5x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061(5x-2)}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(5x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sin}\u2061(5x-2)\\text{d}x & = \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(5x-2)+C & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
